as/texas/king-county"],["ARC or PLC in King County","/arc-plc/texas/king-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 40 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 226% of normal in March to April, then just 31% in September to October 2025. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 38% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 16018 had its driest year in 1956 at 36% of normal.</p>"}
